Note that the devteam have suggested using sys/winnt/Install.nt along 
with gcc -mno-cygwin.  I've only tried the Unix approach myself.

This doesn't diagnose your problem, but I put up a working patch at
  http://math.berkeley.edu/~schneck/cygwin/nethack/nethackcyg.patch

I just downloaded, gunzipped, and untarred the nethack source, went into
the top directory, put the patch there, and ran

patch -p1 < nethackcyg.patch
sh sys/unix/setup.sh
make install
/usr/games/nethack

and it works fine, at least in an rxvt window.  This may not help 
you if you want X, or if you want cursor or alt keys.

